acceptance_criteria: "Every MCP declared key resolves to a CLI flag, via a shared name or a registered alias; A parity gate fails when an MCP declared key has no CLI flag or alias that accepts it; The unknown-option recovery names the accepted flag for a known cross-surface synonym"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: "1. Read the pm_update declared keys, which list linkedFile and linkedTest  2. Run pm update <id> --linked-file path=a.ts  3. Refusal: Unknown option --linked-file"
resolution: The SDK exports deterministic MCP-to-CLI parity verification; create/update accept contract-derived --linked-file and --linked-test aliases; all 43/48 parameters remain executable with zero findings.
expected_result: "One name per concept across MCP and CLI, or an alias so a contract-derived name always parses."
actual_result: All 43 create and 48 update MCP parameters resolve to executable CLI flags or aliases; --linked-file and --linked-test parse through create/update and the exported parity verifier reports zero findings.
